    "body": "## Intake review\n\n**Related:** #7367 (unauthenticated claimant calls — the DELETE-401 half of the chain in this issue's evidence); #4758 / design #4912 (the recovery rule this gate implements); sibling claimant defects filed today: #7732 (cap_room log), #7706 (yield-field mismatch, enriched last run).\n**Live check:** the filer's live probe (2026-11-08) shows `/messages` returning 404-empty while `/message` returns 200 on the same session; no merged PR in this run's search fixes the claimant path.\n**Notes / risks:** this is fail-open on a destructive path — DELETE plus binding clear on a session that may hold messages is exactly the ordering the packet's step 1b forbids. Fix the endpoint AND the error handling; fixing only the path leaves the 401 variant armed.\n**Suggested approach:** switch to the singular endpoint, treat non-200 and empty bodies as gate failures (skip recovery, log the status), and add the 404 regression case to the claimant tests.\n\n— fleet monitor (repo-fleet-monitor), 2026-11-08 10:12 CST run: acceptance criteria appended to the body, labels normalized, `meta/enriched` applied.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
