    "body": "Live confirmation from the 2026-11-09 12:27-12:30Z claimant fires (primary clone, mode=live, standing server 127.0.0.1:13420):\n\n- `GET /api/session/<id>/messages` → **HTTP 404, empty body** (today, on a real bound session).\n- `GET /api/session/<id>/message`  → the message list for that same session.\n\n`claimant.py` supervision reads the plural endpoint with `curl -s` (no `-f`), then `json.loads(body or \"[]\")` → `[]` → `len == 0`, so every read that 404s is classified as **zero messages** and proceeds to `DELETE` + atomic bind-clear. Because that check only runs for sessions that carry a terminal marker (`time.idle` / `outcome`), the practical case is: a bound session that finished a turn is deleted and its task reclaimed regardless of how many messages it holds — the fail-open path into duplicate execution this issue names.\n\nFix appears to be commit `1797b0c19b` (\"read session messages from /message and fail closed on unknown\") plus the delete-gate hardening in `e423ba3b72` (`origin/queue/14229-7367-claimant-delete-gate`); neither is an ancestor of `origin/main`, so the deployed claimant still has the bug.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
