    "body": "<!-- agent-note:v1 agent=triage-step state=triaged at=2026-11-10T06:40:00Z -->\n🤖 **Agent note** · triaged\n- **Agent:** triage-step\n- **State:** triaged\n- **Work kind:** task/small-fix\n- **Priority:** priority/high — Brief line 1: keep the fleet itself able to work. The claimant's fail-open zero-message gate can clear a live session's binding and launch a duplicate, a fleet-stalling failure mode; the issue already carried priority/high and it stands.\n- **Effort:** effort/s (already on the issue)\n- **First step:** In pm-stack/opencode-claimant/claimant.py, point the zero-message gate at the singular /api/session/<id>/message endpoint and treat any non-200, empty-body, or wrong-shape read as UNKNOWN — never zero, never gone — and correct the stub in test/test_claimant.py:75 to the writer's shapes. This is Phase 2 of design #7770; do not re-scope or split it.\n- **Acceptance check:** A 200 from the singular /message path whose data list is empty is the only read that counts as zero messages; 404/401/empty/wrong-shape reads block recovery instead of triggering DELETE + bind-clear, pinned by tests using the corrected stub.\n- **Packet:** No new fix packet enqueued: the design-architect note on this issue (2026-11-08) records it as Phase 2 of design #7770 with its existing queue lifecycle unchanged and no new packet to be filed.\n",
